# ─── Self-update SFTP account, local build only ───────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to cmake/SelfUpdateCredentials.cmake (WITHOUT .template) and
# fill in the values. That name is gitignored: this repository is public, so the
# account never goes into a tracked file. CI builds get the same values from
# repository secrets — see .github/workflows/ci.yml.
#
# This is the SECOND SFTP account, not the EngineContent one
# (cmake/EngineContentCredentials.cmake): the one holding editor builds, and it
# must be READ-ONLY. Whatever is filled in here is compiled into the shipped
# editor, where anyone can read it out of the binary, so a write-capable login
# here would let anyone hand every editor out there code to run. The editor
# refuses a login that is the same as the EngineContent one.
#
# src/HE_SelfUpdate/CMakeLists.txt includes the copy when it exists, and what it
# sets here wins over everything else on this machine. Having no file at all is a
# normal state: Help ▸ Check for Updates… then says "not configured", unless the
# HE_SELFUPDATE_* variables are set in the editor's environment at run time
# (which always replace the compiled-in account as a whole).
#
# Plain set(), deliberately — NOT set(... CACHE ...). A cache set without FORCE
# does nothing once the entry already exists, so in a build directory you had
# configured before, a CACHE version of this file would be silently ignored.
# (The CMakeLists declares those cache entries BEFORE including this file, which
# is what lets these plain set()s win on a fresh build directory too.)
#
# After copying this file: configure once. The build system re-checks for this
# file's arrival on its own (file(GLOB … CONFIGURE_DEPENDS)), and the configure
# output then names the account — "HorizonSelfUpdate: update account
# <user>@<host>:22". If it still says "not configured", nothing here took.
#
# Rotation: change the password here AND in the SELFUPDATE_PASSWORD secret.
set(HE_SELFUPDATE_HOST     "")   # e.g. "access-xxxxxxx.webspace-host.com"
set(HE_SELFUPDATE_PORT     "22")
set(HE_SELFUPDATE_USER     "")   # the READ-ONLY login
set(HE_SELFUPDATE_PASSWORD "")
set(HE_SELFUPDATE_BASEPATH "")   # "" = the account's own root (holds packages/, preview-packages/)
